Question: How do I enable automount on boot?
Session: session-123
Model: gemma3:1b
Latency: 842ms
Cache: miss

Use systemd automount units to mount the share on-demand.

Sources:
[1] systemd.automount - Automount unit configuration
    /var/lib/linux-rag/man/systemd.automount
    Create an automount unit pointing at your mount unit.

[2] fstab best practices
    /var/lib/linux-rag/wiki/fstab-best-practices
    Use noauto,x-systemd.automount to enable lazy mounting.
